    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d27">

                <pb facs="0037" n="27" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg27"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">856D.6363/807: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Batavia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Foote</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Batavia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-01-22T15:00:00+07:30">January 22, 1941—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 22—6:57 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Reference is made to my telegram of January 21, 11 a.m. Official reaction to the
                    Japanese proposals is that they are ridiculous and absurd and form no basis
                    whatsoever for discussion or negotiation. The head of the Netherlands delegation
                    has just informed me that <pb facs="0038" n="28" xml:id="pg28"/> he will deliver
                    his idea of an agenda to the Japanese delegation within the next few days but
                    that he will neither refer to nor take any notice whatever of the Japanese
                    suggestions which are regarded as being nearly duplicates of the demands that
                    the Japanese made on French Indochina. He also informed me in strict confidence
                    that he will endeavor to prolong the negotiations as long as possible in order
                    to give Great Britain more time to bring about a change in the situation in
                    Europe.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Foote</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
